Recently, someone posted, asking for a nethack guide to cover the ground 
between the vague doc and the ultra-specific spoiler file.  The smart ass
in me told him "Sure, it's called rec.games.hack."  He responded, "Then
why did a kajillion people ask me to e-mail them any reponses."  So I shame-
facedly offer to answer his questions, because he was right.  This newsgroup
has gotten a little lofty lately.  Which is okay, as long as we realize that
everyone hasn't been playing forever, and not ignore their questions, or make
them embarassed to ask.

The following is a list of question I received that might be of use to 
beginning players.  Technically, there are spoilers.  Nethack gurus can
probably skip it entirely, or read it and add to it (hint).


1. What does call scroll *** mean?
	After you read a scroll, one of three thing can happen.  First, the 
effect is so obvious nethack names it for you (fire, genocide).  Second, the 
effect is somewhat more subtle, but with experience you can figure it out.
(silver glow = enchant armor).  Finally, you have a strange feeling for a 
moment.  This means you have no idea what happened.

2. What is the best character?
	For a beginner, you need brute physical skills (Str, Con, Dex) and a
good weapon.  This will allow to survive through hack 'n' slash while learning
about the games.  The barbarian has the best stats, but the valkyrie isn't far
behind, and with a little luck, can make a killer character.  The samurai is 
up there as well, with good stats, weapon, and armor.  The only drawback is thathe is lawful, and therefore somewhat more restricted.  Any of these will server
you well until you have the know how to play with some of the more finesse 
classes.

3. How do I get hit points?
	With a high Con character, you should hit 50 between levels 4 and 6.
Also, try quaffing a potion of extra healing at full HP.

4. The monster keep kicking my ass.  How do I avoid this?
	Run away!!!  Seriously, there are just times you've got to run.  I 
usually start thinking about it a 50% of my HP.

5. How do I pray?
	The # key (Shift-3) access extended commands on most systems.  Try
various letters after the # and see.  # p prays.

6. How do I feed my pet?
	Lower case t is the throw command.  Find the inventory letter of what
you want to feed you pet, wait until you pet is in a straight or diagnal line
with you, and t the food.  Pets like tripe and fresh dead things.

7. What do I do with sinks?
	Ignore them mostly.  Or if you want, drop a ring in these to get a clue
as to the rings nature.  You'll probably (95%) lose the ring though.

8. What do I do with non-hostile monsters?
	Be grateful.  There are already enough things out there to kill you.
By the way, these are like aligned monster, technically your friends.  They 
don't do much.

9. Does it matter what ring-finger you use?
	No.  Just nethack's way of keeping track.

10. What about the castle I keep hearing about?
	Forget about it.  It will be a while before you see it.  Worry about 
other things for now.

11. What does naming you weapon do?
	For the most part, nothing.  Names are used to designate artifacts that
you can acquire in various ways.  You can, however, name a elven dagger Sting
or a two-handed sword Orcrist and get an (minor) artifact useful against Orcs.
	

Feel free to e-mail me more questions, and if I get enough, I'll make another
post like this.
	


